Article 34

(1) In addition to general investigation officials, investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children in this Regional Regulation, may also be conducted by civil servant investigators as referred to in the Criminal

Procedure Code.

(2) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1), are certain civil servant officials within the regional government who are appointed by authorized officials in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations

(3) In carrying out investigation duties, the investigation officials as referred to in paragraph (1), are authorized:

a. to receive reports or complaints from a person regarding criminal acts of violence against women and children;
b. to take initial action at that time at the scene and conduct examination;
c. to interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identification;
d. to seize objects and/or letters;
e. to take fingerprints and photograph a person;
f. to summon people to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. to bring in experts needed in connection with case examination;
h. to terminate investigation after receiving instructions from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify the public prosecutor, suspect or their family; and/or
i. to take other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be accounted for.
(4) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1), shall notify the commencement of investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the public prosecutor through investigators of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.
